1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,543
Chapter eleven — the agent loop.

2
00:00:03,603 --> 00:00:10,346
The workbench is not an editor. It is the
thing that tells the editor what to do.

3
00:00:10,406 --> 00:00:17,742
Start from a symbol in the code lens.

4
00:00:17,802 --> 00:00:26,048
Runs on binds this module to a
node on the architecture canvas.

5
00:00:26,108 --> 00:00:36,034
Now the code has a place in the system,
and the node has code behind it.

6
00:00:36,094 --> 00:00:44,340
VS Code opens this file at this line
— the exact one, not the folder.

7
00:00:44,400 --> 00:01:01,667
But the useful move is to
write down what is wrong.

8
00:01:01,727 --> 00:01:10,364
A real note, on the exact
symbol it belongs to.

9
00:01:10,424 --> 00:01:19,959
That annotation is not a
sticky note in your browser.

10
00:01:20,019 --> 00:01:27,463
It lands in a worklist on
disk, keyed to this repository.

11
00:01:27,523 --> 00:01:33,965
The MCP sidecar serves that list to
Claude Code as zen underscore worklist —

12
00:01:34,025 --> 00:01:42,468
so a session can pull what you flagged,
with the call graph you flagged it from.

13
00:01:42,528 --> 00:01:53,480
From here it goes two ways. First, file it.

14
00:01:53,540 --> 00:02:04,483
A real GitHub issue on this repository, with the
symbol, the location and the captured context.

15
00:02:04,543 --> 00:02:12,481
Second: hand it to an agent.

16
00:02:12,541 --> 00:02:21,484
That starts a headless Claude Code
run, in this repository, on this item.

17
00:02:21,544 --> 00:02:54,639
Not a nudge to your open session — its
own run, so nothing interrupts you.

18
00:02:54,699 --> 00:03:06,156
It is reading the file, the callers and your note,
then making the smallest change that fixes it.

19
00:03:06,216 --> 00:03:16,662
And it reports back: what it changed,
and the diff stat to prove it.

20
00:03:16,722 --> 00:03:23,665
The same summary is posted onto the issue.

21
00:03:23,725 --> 00:03:28,163
Then close the loop.

22
00:03:28,223 --> 00:03:37,168
Resolve marks it done here and
closes the issue on GitHub.

23
00:03:37,228 --> 00:03:47,553
Flag it, file it, fix it, close it
— without leaving the system view.

24
00:03:47,613 --> 00:03:57,059
And it works the other way too: derive an
architecture from the repository itself.

25
00:03:57,119 --> 00:04:04,122
The agent writes the code. The workbench
keeps the whole system in view.
